Package: tidyvisor
Title: A Statistical Adviser for Tidy Ecological Analyses
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: Advice before the analysis and interpretation after it, shared
    by a family of ecological packages. Given data and a question,
    'tidyvisor' recommends the analysis, the test and the plots, checks the
    data for the usual pitfalls and gives the code to run; given a fitted
    result, it explains the numbers and the figure in plain sentences, with
    its reasons, so the advice can be checked and overruled. The knowledge
    lives in the packages that do the analyses, each of which registers an
    adviser: 'tidydiversity' for community ecology (which ordination and
    which test) and 'tidymapr' for spatial ecology (species distributions,
    the spread of invasions and epidemics, range shifts and spatial
    autocorrelation).
